Package: phonActivR
Type: Package
Title: Simulating and Testing Prosodic-Constraint (Delta) Hypotheses in
    Cross-Linguistic Spoken Word Recognition
Version: 0.2.0
Date: 2026-09-26
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yu-Cheng", "Lin", email = "yucheng.lin@utrgv.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5905-6928")),
    person("Hitomi", "Kambara", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5302-1305"))
  )
Description: A pure-R implementation of a compact, bounded lateral-inhibition
    competition model in the interactive-activation family (cf. McClelland &
    Rumelhart, 1981) for generating qualitative predictions about phonological
    competition in spoken word recognition. It is not the TRACE model: it omits
    TRACE's feature and word levels, time-slice reduplication, time-varying input,
    and top-down feedback, and its parameter defaults are its own. Introduces the
    delta parameter, which operationalizes cross-linguistic prosodic processing
    constraints (e.g., moraic,
    syllabic) as temporal delays on sub-unit
    activation; delta shifts simulated competition monotonically but its leverage
    is modest relative to competitor-overlap structure. Supports item-level
    simulation across full experimental stimulus sets with automatic phonological
    overlap computation from a binary adaptation, constructed by the package
    authors, of the seven McClelland-Elman (1986) feature dimensions (the
    original TRACE II specification is an eight-level continuum over 15
    phonemes), used here as a similarity metric only. Includes paradigm-agnostic empirical overlay functions
    for normalizing and superimposing model predictions onto time-course data from
    mouse-tracking, eye-tracking, ERP, or any paradigm producing a time-varying
    competition measure. Designed for cross-linguistic and bilingual spoken word
    recognition research.
